---
description: |
  Summarizes HarfangLab HTTP Activity (`class_uid` 4002) into one event per
  window, endpoint, destination, HTTP method, and response code. Events of
  other classes pass through unchanged.

  Each summary is an HTTP Activity event with the OCSF aggregation
  attributes: `count` holds the number of requests, `start_time` and
  `end_time` the times of the first and last one, `duration` the time between
  them, and `time` equals `start_time`. All times are epoch milliseconds, like
  HarfangLab's.

  HarfangLab names the requesting endpoint in `src_endpoint` and sends no
  `device`. The URL path, query string, and full URL appear only if all
  requests of the summary had the same value, so the summary of a single
  request keeps them. `unmapped.distinct_url_paths` holds the number of
  distinct paths and `unmapped.url_paths` the first 10 of them in sorted
  order. A summary keeps at most 10 paths and a query string only if all
  requests had the same one, so detections on URL paths and query strings
  need the full events in a data lake.
  Without a uniform path, the summary has no `url.path` and no
  `url.url_string`, which OCSF requires at least one of.

  The summary takes the activity, severity, and status names, the endpoint,
  and the metadata from the first event of the endpoint with the same IDs in
  the window.

  Windows close on the wall clock every `window`, and every summary covers at
  most one `window` of event time. The package description explains the
  windowing, the memory it needs, and how a SIEM counts summaries.
args:
  named:
    - name: window
      type: duration
      default: 5min
      description: Width of the summary windows, in processing and event time.
---

// `$window` names the argument only outside the `window` block.
if class_uid == 4002 {
  _host = src_endpoint?.uid? else src_endpoint?.name?
  _bucket = from_epoch(time? * 1ms).floor($window)
  // Every group key and aggregate costs memory per summary. The values in
  // `_ids` are few per endpoint, so the summaries group by their digest and
  // take them from one context record per endpoint and digest. The endpoint
  // and metadata come from the first event of the context.
  _ids = hash_xxh3([src_endpoint?.name?, src_endpoint?.hostname?,
    activity_id?, activity_name?, severity_id?, severity?, status_id?,
    status?, type_uid?])
  // A string has no `min` and `max`, so the summary compares digests to find
  // out whether all requests had the same one.
  _query = uint(hash_xxh3(http_request?.url?.query_string?), base=16)
  _url = uint(hash_xxh3(http_request?.url?.url_string?), base=16)
  window size=$window {
    fork_merge {
      summarize _host, _bucket, _ids, http_request?.http_method?,
        http_request?.url?.hostname?, http_request?.url?.scheme?,
        http_request?.url?.port?, http_response?.code?,
        dst_endpoint?.ip?, dst_endpoint?.hostname?, dst_endpoint?.port?,
        count=count(), start_time=min(time?), end_time=max(time?),
        _paths=distinct(http_request?.url?.path?),
        _path_count=count(http_request?.url?.path?),
        _query_first=first(http_request?.url?.query_string?),
        _query_min=min(_query), _query_max=max(_query),
        _url_first=first(http_request?.url?.url_string?),
        _url_min=min(_url), _url_max=max(_url)
    }, {
      summarize _host, _ids, _context=first({
        activity_id: activity_id?,
        activity_name: activity_name?,
        severity: severity?,
        severity_id: severity_id?,
        status: status?,
        status_id: status_id?,
        type_uid: type_uid?,
        metadata: metadata?,
        src_endpoint: src_endpoint?,
      })
    }
    // The context of an endpoint and digest sorts before its summaries, so a
    // running `first` hands it to each of them.
    sort _host, _ids, _context? == null
    summarize _host, _ids, _ctx=first(_context?),
      options={mode: "cumulative"}
    where _context? == null
    _same_path = _path_count == 0 or (
      _paths.length() == 1 and _path_count == count)
    this = {
      activity_id: _ctx.activity_id,
      activity_name: _ctx.activity_name,
      category_uid: 4,
      class_uid: 4002,
      metadata: _ctx.metadata,
      severity: _ctx.severity,
      severity_id: _ctx.severity_id,
      status: _ctx.status,
      status_id: _ctx.status_id,
      time: start_time,
      start_time: start_time,
      end_time: end_time,
      duration: end_time - start_time,
      count: count,
      type_uid: _ctx.type_uid,
      http_request: {
        http_method: http_request.http_method,
        url: {
          ...http_request.url,
          path: _paths[0]? if _same_path else null,
          query_string: _query_first if _query_min == _query_max else null,
          url_string: _url_first if _url_min == _url_max else null,
        },
      },
      http_response: http_response,
      dst_endpoint: dst_endpoint,
      src_endpoint: _ctx.src_endpoint,
      unmapped: {
        distinct_url_paths: _paths.length(),
        url_paths: _paths.sort().slice(end=10),
      },
    }
    drop_null_fields
  }
}
